---
source: crates/surfaces/cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
Run the project's test runners and record which entities their tests prove

Usage: specforge collect [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --path <PATH>
          A path inside the project (the nearest directory at or above it holding specforge.json; none: the directory itself, with the default configuration)
          
          [default: .]

      --runner <NAME>
          Collector to use (e.g. cargo-test). Detected from project files if omitted

      --no-run
          Parse the runner's existing report instead of running it

      --report <FILE>
          Report files to parse instead of running the runner (implies --no-run)

      --dry-run
          Plan a writing collector's edits and write none of them

      --yes
          Run the declared test command without asking (for CI)

      --effects <EFFECTS>
          Whether the run performs, reuses or replays an http or process effect (ADR 0337): `check`, and a `collect` whose collector reads the checks' outcomes, run `auto` when someone can answer outside CI; `collect` lends its collectors `online`; every other run `cached`

          Possible values:
          - online: Performed when granted; the answer is journaled
          - auto:   A fresh record; else performed when approved; else not performed
          - cached: A fresh record; else not performed
          - replay: Any record, expired or not; else a miss

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human or json
          
          [default: human]
          [possible values: human, json]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
